From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:39:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] core: keep Mutter's D-Bus services from sandboxed apps

Mutter exports its services on the session bus connection the shell
shares, so an app whose bus proxy lets it talk to any name the shell
owns, such as org.freedesktop.Notifications, can call every one of
them. OpenWaylandConnection on the service channel handed such an app
a Wayland connection that counts as the compositor's own, outside its
sandbox, and the idle monitor told it the exact idle time and let it
remove the watches of others.

meta_dbus_guard_interface() refuses every method of an interface to
sandboxed callers except the ones listed as open, judging the caller
like a Wayland client. The service channel, input mapping, the
accessibility services and every session manager, which covers screen
recording, remote control, input capture and color calibration, get it
with nothing open, so the owner of the portal's or the screencast
service's name must run outside a sandbox as well. The display
configuration gets it with its reading methods open, in place of a
list of the changing ones.

The idle monitor stays open, held to what ext-idle-notify-v1 gives
sandboxed clients: idle times under ten seconds read as none, idle
watches wait at least ten seconds, and a watch for the user coming back
only fires after such an idle time. A watch can only be removed by the
connection that added it.

The apps a permission covers are read from the threads that authorize
calls, so they are now locked.

Upstream-Status: luft-only Luft's sandbox model; upstream leaves these services to the session bus
